# Dynamics/transport research handoff

2026-10-04. Completed declared scoped branch: 43 interfaces, 35 A and 8 B, three suggested pairs, maximum 14 items per page. The coordinator owns final homes and category integration. These are research modules/proposed interfaces, not production items, publication or an engine transition.

The three full proof bodies are equilibrium-response.md T0–T6, channels-and-generators.md C0–C5, detailed-balance-models.md G0–G5. They supply finite recurrence/Cesaro dephasing, exact finite-time Kubo with factorial remainder, spectral distribution FDT including the zero-frequency qualification, bounded C-star and normal trace-class response with precise strong-domain sufficient conditions, integrability-qualified observable variance Green–Kubo and pure-point nonintegrability obstruction. Channel mathematics includes full finite Choi/Kraus equivalence, Schwarz/trace contraction, explicit ancillary/preparation/memory counterexamples, finite GKSL sufficient **and necessary** theorems, continuous-time-dependent finite propagators and precise entropy statements. The final branch proves specified GNS detailed balance, finite scalar-kernel gap and trace relaxation, Gibbs jump/commuting KL, fixed-dissipator response, exactly solved thermal qubit and explicitly monitored classical transport variance.

Three postulates and three physical theorems make unitary/control/effective-bath interpretation conditional. Initial product preparation, finite isolated evolution, processed entropy, effective bath and recorded jump law are distinct model premises. All quantity assignments and units remain explicit in the bodies. No measurements, calibrated parameter values or experiments were invented. Background literature links are identified as context, never newly retrieved full-proof reading or replacements for local mathematical arguments.

supplier-map.json records 17 exact external mathematical/physical contracts, current file hashes, hypotheses, actual consumer IDs, publication/research/axiom status and bounded reading extents. Root functional-analysis planned permission is a catalog disposition, not automatic proof certification. NRQM finite/countable partial-trace sources were inspected; the finite case is reproduced locally. G4 explicitly consumes frozen CSM D14's genuine joint-path construction and retains full AC, instead of inferring a path law from Poisson marginals. Root trace-cyclicity reading is restricted to its bounded-trace proof branch. No new external whole text was needed and no failed retrieval is claimed.

The coordinator reported actual reading of every T0–T6/C0–C5/G0–G5 proof body, checked the required sign/domain/scope branches, and requested bounded repairs. Those repairs are applied: T0's entropy reference points to C5; amplitude damping is stated as a channel that need not increase entropy; finite trace duality includes its own spectral SVD/polar construction; the dc obstruction treats real symmetrized G as well as C; real retarded PV limit has its compact C1 test proof; G4 has the exact joint-path supplier. This report records that bounded peer reading, not independent whole-supplier or production acceptance.

